  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Decision\\n\\nWhen a stored observation cursor is rejected, this workspace's integration should expect a **fail-closed `InvalidCursorError` from `@ordarium/core` — `error.code === \\\"INVALID_CURSOR\\\"`** (\\\"The change cursor is not a valid durable position; refusing to guess a resume point\\\"). The rejection is evaluated against the **ledger-global position (`Record A` semantics), not a per-consumer position (`Record B`)**.\\n\\n## What \\\"stored observation cursor\\\" is\\n\\nThe pinned kernel's change-feed contract (`@ordarium/core` v1.3.1) calls this surface *observation*:\\n\\n- `OrdariumStateStore.changes()` — \\\"Incremental observation of committed state revisions **after a durable position** (ORD-BOOT-0)\\\".\\n- `StateChangePage.cursor` — \\\"Opaque, **filter-independent** durable position of the last delivered change… a consumer reaches the end of the feed and still holds a durable resume position.\\\"\\n\\nA consumer persists that `cursor` across restarts; that persisted value is the stored observation cursor.\\n\\n## Why the rejection is global (Record A), not per-consumer (Record B)\\n\\nThe two local records are a genuine contradiction: `docs/engineering/09-error-contract-a.md` says the cursor",
